{"candidate_output": "```python\ndef odd_values_string(s):\n    return ''.join(s[i] for i in range(len(s)) if i % 2 == 0)\n```", "case_id": "code_mbpp-b08d564f49eba222", "context": "assert odd_values_string('abcdef') == 'ace'\nassert odd_values_string('python') == 'pto'\nassert odd_values_string('data') == 'dt'\nassert odd_values_string('lambs') == 'lms'", "difficulty": "medium", "generator_id": "gpt-4.1-nano", "group_id": "mbpp-8f1f64db81c4", "meta": {"oracle_detail": "tests passed", "oracle_method": "code:exec"}, "origin": "real", "reference": "def odd_values_string(str):\n  result = \"\" \n  for i in range(len(str)):\n    if i % 2 == 0:\n      result = result + str[i]\n  return result", "reference_provenance": "MBPP reference solution", "rubric_id": "", "rubric_version": "", "schema_version": "1.0.0", "source": "MBPP", "source_license": "CC-BY-4.0", "task_class": "code", "task_input": "Write a python function to remove the characters which have odd index values of a given string."}
