{"candidate_output": "```python\ndef add_pairwise(tup):\n    return tuple(tup[i] + tup[i + 1] for i in range(len(tup) - 1))\n\n# Test cases\nassert add_pairwise((1, 5, 7, 8, 10)) == (6, 12, 15, 18)\nassert add_pairwise((2, 6, 8, 9, 11)) == (8, 14, 17, 20)\nassert add_pairwise((3, 7, 9, 10, 12)) == (10, 16, 19, 22)\n```", "case_id": "code_mbpp-941b56fd8fcc6d67", "context": "assert add_pairwise((1, 5, 7, 8, 10)) == (6, 12, 15, 18)\nassert add_pairwise((2, 6, 8, 9, 11)) == (8, 14, 17, 20)\nassert add_pairwise((3, 7, 9, 10, 12)) == (10, 16, 19, 22)", "difficulty": "medium", "generator_id": "gpt-4o-mini", "group_id": "mbpp-30eec89ddd9c", "meta": {"oracle_detail": "tests passed", "oracle_method": "code:exec"}, "origin": "real", "reference": "def add_pairwise(test_tup):\n  res = tuple(i + j for i, j in zip(test_tup, test_tup[1:]))\n  return (res) ", "reference_provenance": "MBPP reference solution", "rubric_id": "", "rubric_version": "", "schema_version": "1.0.0", "source": "MBPP", "source_license": "CC-BY-4.0", "task_class": "code", "task_input": "Write a function to find the pairwise addition of the neighboring elements of the given tuple."}
