{"candidate_output": "```python\ndef pancake_sort(arr):\n    def flip(sublist, k):\n        return sublist[:k][::-1] + sublist[k:]\n    \n    n = len(arr)\n    for size in range(n, 1, -1):\n        # Find index of the maximum element in arr[0..size-1]\n        max_idx = arr.index(max(arr[:size]))\n        if max_idx != size - 1:\n            # Flip max element to front if it's not already at front\n            if max_idx != 0:\n                arr = flip(arr, max_idx + 1)\n            # Flip it to its correct position\n            arr = flip(arr, size)\n    return arr\n```", "case_id": "code_mbpp-c8effe72447ad178", "context": "assert pancake_sort([15, 79, 25, 38, 69]) == [15, 25, 38, 69, 79]\nassert pancake_sort([98, 12, 54, 36, 85]) == [12, 36, 54, 85, 98]\nassert pancake_sort([41, 42, 32, 12, 23]) == [12, 23, 32, 41, 42]", "difficulty": "medium", "generator_id": "gpt-4.1-nano", "group_id": "mbpp-2c7d5490e605", "meta": {"oracle_detail": "tests passed", "oracle_method": "code:exec"}, "origin": "real", "reference": "def pancake_sort(nums):\n    arr_len = len(nums)\n    while arr_len > 1:\n        mi = nums.index(max(nums[0:arr_len]))\n        nums = nums[mi::-1] + nums[mi+1:len(nums)]\n        nums = nums[arr_len-1::-1] + nums[arr_len:len(nums)]\n        arr_len -= 1\n    return nums", "reference_provenance": "MBPP reference solution", "rubric_id": "", "rubric_version": "", "schema_version": "1.0.0", "source": "MBPP", "source_license": "CC-BY-4.0", "task_class": "code", "task_input": "Write a function to sort a list of elements."}
