{"candidate_output": "```python\ndef odd_Equivalent(binary_str, rotations):\n    n = len(binary_str)\n    # Convert string to list of integers for easy manipulation\n    bits = list(map(int, binary_str))\n    count = 0\n\n    for i in range(n):\n        # Determine the position after rotations\n        # The bit at position i moves to (i + rotations) % n\n        new_pos = (i + rotations) % n\n        # The bit at new position after rotation\n        rotated_bit = bits[new_pos]\n        # Count if the rotated bit is odd (which is 1)\n        if rotated_bit == 1:\n            count += 1\n    return count\n\n# Test cases\nassert odd_Equivalent(\"011001\",6) == 3\nassert odd_Equivalent(\"11011\",5) == 4\nassert odd_Equivalent(\"1010\",4) == 2\n```", "case_id": "code_mbpp-b41e56b8da079629", "context": "assert odd_Equivalent(\"011001\",6) == 3\nassert odd_Equivalent(\"11011\",5) == 4\nassert odd_Equivalent(\"1010\",4) == 2", "difficulty": "medium", "generator_id": "gpt-4.1-nano", "group_id": "mbpp-0fd42b3f73c4", "meta": {"oracle_detail": "tests passed", "oracle_method": "code:exec"}, "origin": "real", "reference": "def odd_Equivalent(s,n): \n    count=0\n    for i in range(0,n): \n        if (s[i] == '1'): \n            count = count + 1\n    return count ", "reference_provenance": "MBPP reference solution", "rubric_id": "", "rubric_version": "", "schema_version": "1.0.0", "source": "MBPP", "source_license": "CC-BY-4.0", "task_class": "code", "task_input": "Write a python function to find the number of numbers with an odd value when rotating a binary string the given number of times."}
