{"candidate_output": "```python\ndef get_Char(s):\n    total_ascii = sum(ord(c) for c in s)\n    return chr((total_ascii % 26) + ord('a'))\n```", "case_id": "code_mbpp-6bbb79c33baba640", "context": "assert get_Char(\"abc\") == \"f\"\nassert get_Char(\"gfg\") == \"t\"\nassert get_Char(\"ab\") == \"c\"", "difficulty": "medium", "generator_id": "gpt-4.1-nano", "group_id": "mbpp-bbb965ab0c80", "meta": {"oracle_detail": "exit 1", "oracle_method": "code:exec"}, "origin": "real", "reference": "def get_Char(strr):  \n    summ = 0\n    for i in range(len(strr)): \n        summ += (ord(strr[i]) - ord('a') + 1)  \n    if (summ % 26 == 0): \n        return ord('z') \n    else: \n        summ = summ % 26\n        return chr(ord('a') + summ - 1)", "reference_provenance": "MBPP reference solution", "rubric_id": "", "rubric_version": "", "schema_version": "1.0.0", "source": "MBPP", "source_license": "CC-BY-4.0", "task_class": "code", "task_input": "Write a python function to find the character made by adding the ASCII value of all the characters of the given string modulo 26."}
{"candidate_output": "```python\ndef maximize_elements(t1, t2):\n    return tuple((max(a, b), max(c, d)) for (a, c), (b, d) in zip(t1, t2))\n\n# Test cases\nassert maximize_elements(((1, 3), (4, 5), (2, 9), (1, 10)), ((6, 7), (3, 9), (1, 1), (7, 3))) == ((6, 7), (4, 9), (2, 9), (7, 10))\nassert maximize_elements(((2, 4), (5, 6), (3, 10), (2, 11)), ((7, 8), (4, 10), (2, 2), (8, 4))) == ((7, 8), (5, 10), (3, 10), (8, 11))\nassert maximize_elements(((3, 5), (6, 7), (4, 11), (3, 12)), ((8, 9), (5, 11), (3, 3), (9, 5))) == ((8, 9), (6, 11), (4, 11), (9, 12))\n```", "case_id": "code_mbpp-9674b1a037f5878d", "context": "assert maximize_elements(((1, 3), (4, 5), (2, 9), (1, 10)), ((6, 7), (3, 9), (1, 1), (7, 3))) == ((6, 7), (4, 9), (2, 9), (7, 10))\nassert maximize_elements(((2, 4), (5, 6), (3, 10), (2, 11)), ((7, 8), (4, 10), (2, 2), (8, 4))) == ((7, 8), (5, 10), (3, 10), (8, 11))\nassert maximize_elements(((3, 5), (6, 7), (4, 11), (3, 12)), ((8, 9), (5, 11), (3, 3), (9, 5))) == ((8, 9), (6, 11), (4, 11), (9, 12))", "difficulty": "medium", "generator_id": "gpt-4o-mini", "group_id": "mbpp-7c252ab334fb", "meta": {"oracle_detail": "tests passed", "oracle_method": "code:exec"}, "origin": "real", "reference": "def maximize_elements(test_tup1, test_tup2):\n  res = tuple(tuple(max(a, b) for a, b in zip(tup1, tup2))\n   for tup1, tup2 in zip(test_tup1, test_tup2))\n  return (res) ", "reference_provenance": "MBPP reference solution", "rubric_id": "", "rubric_version": "", "schema_version": "1.0.0", "source": "MBPP", "source_license": "CC-BY-4.0", "task_class": "code", "task_input": "Write a function to maximize the given two tuples."}
{"candidate_output": "```python\ndef min_of_three(a, b, c):\n    return min(a, b, c)\n```", "case_id": "code_mbpp-8ac34e7b037a1010", "context": "assert min_of_three(10,20,0)==0\nassert min_of_three(19,15,18)==15\nassert min_of_three(-10,-20,-30)==-30", "difficulty": "medium", "generator_id": "gpt-4.1-nano", "group_id": "mbpp-dfe62e836a0a", "meta": {"oracle_detail": "tests passed", "oracle_method": "code:exec"}, "origin": "real", "reference": "def min_of_three(a,b,c): \n      if (a <= b) and (a <= c): \n        smallest = a \n      elif (b <= a) and (b <= c): \n        smallest = b \n      else: \n        smallest = c \n      return smallest ", "reference_provenance": "MBPP reference solution", "rubric_id": "", "rubric_version": "", "schema_version": "1.0.0", "source": "MBPP", "source_license": "CC-BY-4.0", "task_class": "code", "task_input": "Write a function to find minimum of three numbers."}
{"candidate_output": "```python\ndef max_sum_increasing_subseq(arr, n, i, k):\n    # Calculate the maximum sum of increasing subsequence up to index i\n    max_sum_up_to_i = [0] * (i + 1)\n    \n    for j in range(i + 1):\n        max_sum_up_to_i[j] = arr[j]\n        for l in range(j):\n            if arr[l] < arr[j]:\n                max_sum_up_to_i[j] = max(max_sum_up_to_i[j], max_sum_up_to_i[l] + arr[j])\n    \n    # Now include the kth element\n    max_sum_with_k = 0\n    for j in range(i + 1):\n        if arr[j] < arr[k]:\n            max_sum_with_k = max(max_sum_with_k, max_sum_up_to_i[j] + arr[k])\n    \n    return max_sum_with_k\n\n# Test cases\nassert max_sum_increasing_subseq([1, 101, 2, 3, 100, 4, 5], 7, 4, 6) == 11\nassert max_sum_increasing_subseq([1, 101, 2, 3, 100, 4, 5], 7, 2, 5) == 7\nassert max_sum_increasing_subseq([11, 15, 19, 21, 26, 28, 31], 7, 2, 4) == 71\n```", "case_id": "code_mbpp-8a5cfbbc0058793e", "context": "assert max_sum_increasing_subseq([1, 101, 2, 3, 100, 4, 5 ], 7, 4, 6) == 11\nassert max_sum_increasing_subseq([1, 101, 2, 3, 100, 4, 5 ], 7, 2, 5) == 7\nassert max_sum_increasing_subseq([11, 15, 19, 21, 26, 28, 31], 7, 2, 4) == 71", "difficulty": "medium", "generator_id": "gpt-4o-mini", "group_id": "mbpp-38b83caefa1e", "meta": {"oracle_detail": "tests passed", "oracle_method": "code:exec"}, "origin": "real", "reference": "def max_sum_increasing_subseq(a, n, index, k):\n\tdp = [[0 for i in range(n)] \n\t\t\tfor i in range(n)]\n\tfor i in range(n):\n\t\tif a[i] > a[0]:\n\t\t\tdp[0][i] = a[i] + a[0]\n\t\telse:\n\t\t\tdp[0][i] = a[i]\n\tfor i in range(1, n):\n\t\tfor j in range(n):\n\t\t\tif a[j] > a[i] and j > i:\n\t\t\t\tif dp[i - 1][i] + a[j] > dp[i - 1][j]:\n\t\t\t\t\tdp[i][j] = dp[i - 1][i] + a[j]\n\t\t\t\telse:\n\t\t\t\t\tdp[i][j] = dp[i - 1][j]\n\t\t\telse:\n\t\t\t\tdp[i][j] = dp[i - 1][j]\n\treturn dp[index][k]", "reference_provenance": "MBPP reference solution", "rubric_id": "", "rubric_version": "", "schema_version": "1.0.0", "source": "MBPP", "source_license": "CC-BY-4.0", "task_class": "code", "task_input": "Write a function to find the maximum sum of increasing subsequence from prefix until ith index and also including a given kth element which is after i, i.e., k > i ."}
