{"candidate_output": "```python\ndef largest_neg(numbers):\n    negative_numbers = [num for num in numbers if num < 0]\n    return max(negative_numbers) if negative_numbers else None\n\n# Test cases\nassert largest_neg([1, 2, 3, -4, -6]) == -6\nassert largest_neg([1, 2, 3, -8, -9]) == -9\nassert largest_neg([1, 2, 3, 4, -1]) == -1\n```", "case_id": "code_mbpp-bf4782516b537235", "context": "assert largest_neg([1,2,3,-4,-6]) == -6\nassert largest_neg([1,2,3,-8,-9]) == -9\nassert largest_neg([1,2,3,4,-1]) == -1", "difficulty": "medium", "generator_id": "gpt-4o-mini", "group_id": "mbpp-6d05621ab7cb", "meta": {"oracle_detail": "exit 1", "oracle_method": "code:exec"}, "origin": "real", "reference": "def largest_neg(list1): \n    max = list1[0] \n    for x in list1: \n        if x < max : \n             max = x  \n    return max", "reference_provenance": "MBPP reference solution", "rubric_id": "", "rubric_version": "", "schema_version": "1.0.0", "source": "MBPP", "source_license": "CC-BY-4.0", "task_class": "code", "task_input": "Write a python function to find the largest negative number from the given list."}
