{"candidate_output": "```python\ndef next_power_of_2(n):\n    if n <= 0:\n        return 1\n    # If n is already a power of 2, return n\n    if (n & (n - 1)) == 0:\n        return n\n    # Otherwise, find the next power of 2\n    power = 1\n    while power < n:\n        power <<= 1\n    return power\n```", "case_id": "code_mbpp-071358c3e546b30a", "context": "assert next_power_of_2(0) == 1\nassert next_power_of_2(5) == 8\nassert next_power_of_2(17) == 32", "difficulty": "medium", "generator_id": "gpt-4.1-nano", "group_id": "mbpp-73d3f1ba0625", "meta": {"oracle_detail": "tests passed", "oracle_method": "code:exec"}, "origin": "real", "reference": "def next_power_of_2(n): \n  if n and not n & (n - 1):\n    return n\n\n  count = 0\n  while n != 0: \n    n >>= 1\n    count += 1\n\n  return 1 << count; ", "reference_provenance": "MBPP reference solution", "rubric_id": "", "rubric_version": "", "schema_version": "1.0.0", "source": "MBPP", "source_license": "CC-BY-4.0", "task_class": "code", "task_input": "Write a python function to find the smallest power of 2 greater than or equal to n."}
{"candidate_output": "```python\ndef count_Occurrence(tup, lst):\n    return sum(tup.count(x) for x in lst)\n\n# Test cases\nassert count_Occurrence(('a', 'a', 'c', 'b', 'd'), ['a', 'b']) == 3\nassert count_Occurrence((1, 2, 3, 1, 4, 6, 7, 1, 4), [1, 4, 7]) == 6\nassert count_Occurrence((1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6), [1, 2]) == 2\n```", "case_id": "code_mbpp-d4401bb427fe2e07", "context": "assert count_Occurrence(('a', 'a', 'c', 'b', 'd'),['a', 'b'] ) == 3\nassert count_Occurrence((1, 2, 3, 1, 4, 6, 7, 1, 4),[1, 4, 7]) == 6\nassert count_Occurrence((1,2,3,4,5,6),[1,2]) == 2", "difficulty": "medium", "generator_id": "gpt-4o-mini", "group_id": "mbpp-75c3e223190b", "meta": {"oracle_detail": "tests passed", "oracle_method": "code:exec"}, "origin": "real", "reference": "from collections import Counter \ndef count_Occurrence(tup, lst): \n    count = 0\n    for item in tup: \n        if item in lst: \n            count+= 1 \n    return count  ", "reference_provenance": "MBPP reference solution", "rubric_id": "", "rubric_version": "", "schema_version": "1.0.0", "source": "MBPP", "source_license": "CC-BY-4.0", "task_class": "code", "task_input": "Write a python function to count the occurence of all elements of list in a tuple."}
{"candidate_output": "```python\ndef remove_Occ(s, ch):\n    # Find the index of the first occurrence\n    first_idx = s.find(ch)\n    # Find the index of the last occurrence\n    last_idx = s.rfind(ch)\n    \n    # If the character is not found or occurs only once, handle accordingly\n    if first_idx == -1:\n        return s  # character not found, return original string\n    if first_idx == last_idx:\n        # Only one occurrence, remove it\n        return s[:first_idx] + s[first_idx+1:]\n    # Remove last occurrence first to avoid index shift\n    s = s[:last_idx] + s[last_idx+1:]\n    # Remove first occurrence\n    s = s[:first_idx] + s[first_idx+1:]\n    return s\n```", "case_id": "code_mbpp-3fb32407b1985339", "context": "assert remove_Occ(\"hello\",\"l\") == \"heo\"\nassert remove_Occ(\"abcda\",\"a\") == \"bcd\"\nassert remove_Occ(\"PHP\",\"P\") == \"H\"", "difficulty": "medium", "generator_id": "gpt-4.1-nano", "group_id": "mbpp-4fc82b26aecb", "meta": {"oracle_detail": "tests passed", "oracle_method": "code:exec"}, "origin": "real", "reference": "def remove_Occ(s,ch): \n    for i in range(len(s)): \n        if (s[i] == ch): \n            s = s[0 : i] + s[i + 1:] \n            break\n    for i in range(len(s) - 1,-1,-1):  \n        if (s[i] == ch): \n            s = s[0 : i] + s[i + 1:] \n            break\n    return s ", "reference_provenance": "MBPP reference solution", "rubric_id": "", "rubric_version": "", "schema_version": "1.0.0", "source": "MBPP", "source_license": "CC-BY-4.0", "task_class": "code", "task_input": "Write a python function to remove first and last occurrence of a given character from the string."}
{"candidate_output": "```python\ndef even_Power_Sum(n):\n    return sum((2 * i) ** 5 for i in range(1, n + 1))\n\n# Test cases\nassert even_Power_Sum(2) == 1056\nassert even_Power_Sum(3) == 8832\nassert even_Power_Sum(1) == 32\n```", "case_id": "code_mbpp-3ce054ede2b2f78c", "context": "assert even_Power_Sum(2) == 1056\nassert even_Power_Sum(3) == 8832\nassert even_Power_Sum(1) == 32", "difficulty": "medium", "generator_id": "gpt-4o-mini", "group_id": "mbpp-3635a91e3da8", "meta": {"oracle_detail": "tests passed", "oracle_method": "code:exec"}, "origin": "real", "reference": "def even_Power_Sum(n): \n    sum = 0; \n    for i in range(1,n+1): \n        j = 2*i; \n        sum = sum + (j*j*j*j*j); \n    return sum; ", "reference_provenance": "MBPP reference solution", "rubric_id": "", "rubric_version": "", "schema_version": "1.0.0", "source": "MBPP", "source_license": "CC-BY-4.0", "task_class": "code", "task_input": "Write a python function that takes in an integer n and finds the sum of the first n even natural numbers that are raised to the fifth power."}
