{"candidate_output": "```python\ndef decimal_to_binary(n):\n    if n == 0:\n        return '0'\n    binary_digits = []\n    while n > 0:\n        binary_digits.append(str(n % 2))\n        n //= 2\n    return ''.join(reversed(binary_digits))\n```", "case_id": "code_mbpp-e900b93d1c48dc7c", "context": "assert decimal_to_binary(8) == '1000'\nassert decimal_to_binary(18) == '10010'\nassert decimal_to_binary(7) == '111'", "difficulty": "medium", "generator_id": "gpt-4.1-nano", "group_id": "mbpp-8c1f1046219d", "meta": {"oracle_detail": "tests passed", "oracle_method": "code:exec"}, "origin": "real", "reference": "def decimal_to_binary(n): \n    return bin(n).replace(\"0b\",\"\") ", "reference_provenance": "MBPP reference solution", "rubric_id": "", "rubric_version": "", "schema_version": "1.0.0", "source": "MBPP", "source_license": "CC-BY-4.0", "task_class": "code", "task_input": "Write a function to convert the given decimal number to its binary equivalent, represented as a string with no leading zeros."}
{"candidate_output": "```python\ndef remove_odd(numbers):\n    return [num for num in numbers if num % 2 == 0]\n\n# Test cases\nassert remove_odd([1, 2, 3]) == [2]\nassert remove_odd([2, 4, 6]) == [2, 4, 6]\nassert remove_odd([10, 20, 3]) == [10, 20]\n```", "case_id": "code_mbpp-6b4859d6ce6225cf", "context": "assert remove_odd([1,2,3]) == [2]\nassert remove_odd([2,4,6]) == [2,4,6]\nassert remove_odd([10,20,3]) == [10,20]", "difficulty": "medium", "generator_id": "gpt-4o-mini", "group_id": "mbpp-fabf5b7fedb3", "meta": {"oracle_detail": "tests passed", "oracle_method": "code:exec"}, "origin": "real", "reference": "def remove_odd(l):\n    for i in l:\n        if i % 2 != 0:\n            l.remove(i)\n    return l", "reference_provenance": "MBPP reference solution", "rubric_id": "", "rubric_version": "", "schema_version": "1.0.0", "source": "MBPP", "source_license": "CC-BY-4.0", "task_class": "code", "task_input": "Write a python function to remove odd numbers from a given list."}
{"candidate_output": "```python\ndef highest_Power_of_2(n):\n    # Initialize power to 1 (2^0)\n    power = 1\n    # Keep doubling until the next power exceeds n\n    while power * 2 <= n:\n        power *= 2\n    return power\n```", "case_id": "code_mbpp-e0e8f5be8939704d", "context": "assert highest_Power_of_2(10) == 8\nassert highest_Power_of_2(19) == 16\nassert highest_Power_of_2(32) == 32", "difficulty": "medium", "generator_id": "gpt-4.1-nano", "group_id": "mbpp-ab5e292db649", "meta": {"oracle_detail": "tests passed", "oracle_method": "code:exec"}, "origin": "real", "reference": "def highest_Power_of_2(n): \n    res = 0 \n    for i in range(n, 0, -1): \n        if ((i & (i - 1)) == 0): \n            res = i \n            break \n    return res ", "reference_provenance": "MBPP reference solution", "rubric_id": "", "rubric_version": "", "schema_version": "1.0.0", "source": "MBPP", "source_license": "CC-BY-4.0", "task_class": "code", "task_input": "Write a python function to find the highest power of 2 that is less than or equal to n."}
