{"candidate_output": "```python\ndef find_solution(a, b, n):\n    for x in range(n // a + 1):\n        if (n - a * x) % b == 0:\n            y = (n - a * x) // b\n            return (x, y)\n    return None\n\n# Test cases\nassert find_solution(2, 3, 7) == (2, 1)\nassert find_solution(4, 2, 7) == None\nassert find_solution(1, 13, 17) == (4, 1)\n```", "case_id": "code_mbpp-f7b8f5db38b92dfa", "context": "assert find_solution(2, 3, 7) == (2, 1)\nassert find_solution(4, 2, 7) == None\nassert find_solution(1, 13, 17) == (4, 1)", "difficulty": "medium", "generator_id": "gpt-4o-mini", "group_id": "mbpp-a512db2741cd", "meta": {"oracle_detail": "tests passed", "oracle_method": "code:exec"}, "origin": "real", "reference": "def find_solution(a, b, n):\n\ti = 0\n\twhile i * a <= n:\n\t\tif (n - (i * a)) % b == 0: \n\t\t\treturn (i, (n - (i * a)) // b)\n\t\ti = i + 1\n\treturn None", "reference_provenance": "MBPP reference solution", "rubric_id": "", "rubric_version": "", "schema_version": "1.0.0", "source": "MBPP", "source_license": "CC-BY-4.0", "task_class": "code", "task_input": "Write a function that returns integers x and y that satisfy ax + by = n as a tuple, or return None if no solution exists."}
