{"candidate_output": "```python\ndef sum_of_common_divisors(a, b):\n    def gcd(x, y):\n        while y:\n            x, y = y, x % y\n        return x\n\n    common_divisor_sum = 0\n    g = gcd(a, b)\n    \n    for i in range(1, g + 1):\n        if g % i == 0:\n            common_divisor_sum += i\n            \n    return common_divisor_sum\n\n# Test cases\nassert sum_of_common_divisors(10, 15) == 6\nassert sum_of_common_divisors(100, 150) == 93\nassert sum_of_common_divisors(4, 6) == 3\n```", "case_id": "code_mbpp-063ea31bab710d04", "context": "assert sum(10,15) == 6\nassert sum(100,150) == 93\nassert sum(4,6) == 3", "difficulty": "medium", "generator_id": "gpt-4o-mini", "group_id": "mbpp-65a699905c02", "meta": {"oracle_detail": "exit 1", "oracle_method": "code:exec"}, "origin": "real", "reference": "def sum(a,b): \n    sum = 0\n    for i in range (1,min(a,b)): \n        if (a % i == 0 and b % i == 0): \n            sum += i \n    return sum", "reference_provenance": "MBPP reference solution", "rubric_id": "", "rubric_version": "", "schema_version": "1.0.0", "source": "MBPP", "source_license": "CC-BY-4.0", "task_class": "code", "task_input": "Write a python function to find the sum of common divisors of two given numbers."}
{"candidate_output": "```python\ndef check_occurences(lst):\n    result = {}\n    for t in lst:\n        # Create a key by sorting the tuple to treat (a, b) and (b, a) as the same\n        key = tuple(sorted(t))\n        result[key] = result.get(key, 0) + 1\n    return result\n```", "case_id": "code_mbpp-0ad6c6c7875e322f", "context": "assert check_occurences([(3, 1), (1, 3), (2, 5), (5, 2), (6, 3)] ) == {(1, 3): 2, (2, 5): 2, (3, 6): 1}\nassert check_occurences([(4, 2), (2, 4), (3, 6), (6, 3), (7, 4)] ) == {(2, 4): 2, (3, 6): 2, (4, 7): 1}\nassert check_occurences([(13, 2), (11, 23), (12, 25), (25, 12), (16, 23)] ) == {(2, 13): 1, (11, 23): 1, (12, 25): 2, (16, 23): 1}", "difficulty": "medium", "generator_id": "gpt-4.1-nano", "group_id": "mbpp-f0bc318fb896", "meta": {"oracle_detail": "tests passed", "oracle_method": "code:exec"}, "origin": "real", "reference": "from collections import Counter \ndef check_occurences(test_list):\n  res = dict(Counter(tuple(ele) for ele in map(sorted, test_list)))\n  return  (res) ", "reference_provenance": "MBPP reference solution", "rubric_id": "", "rubric_version": "", "schema_version": "1.0.0", "source": "MBPP", "source_license": "CC-BY-4.0", "task_class": "code", "task_input": "Write a function that takes in a list of tuples and returns a dictionary mapping each unique tuple to the number of times it occurs in the list."}
{"candidate_output": "```python\ndef count_samepair(list1, list2, list3):\n    return sum(1 for a, b, c in zip(list1, list2, list3) if a == b == c)\n\n# Test cases\nassert count_samepair([1,2,3,4,5,6,7,8],[2,2,3,1,2,6,7,9],[2,1,3,1,2,6,7,9])==3\nassert count_samepair([1,2,3,4,5,6,7,8],[2,2,3,1,2,6,7,8],[2,1,3,1,2,6,7,8])==4\nassert count_samepair([1,2,3,4,2,6,7,8],[2,2,3,1,2,6,7,8],[2,1,3,1,2,6,7,8])==5\n```", "case_id": "code_mbpp-85288d2fe286354d", "context": "assert count_samepair([1,2,3,4,5,6,7,8],[2,2,3,1,2,6,7,9],[2,1,3,1,2,6,7,9])==3\nassert count_samepair([1,2,3,4,5,6,7,8],[2,2,3,1,2,6,7,8],[2,1,3,1,2,6,7,8])==4\nassert count_samepair([1,2,3,4,2,6,7,8],[2,2,3,1,2,6,7,8],[2,1,3,1,2,6,7,8])==5", "difficulty": "medium", "generator_id": "gpt-4o-mini", "group_id": "mbpp-d4ee9f58e586", "meta": {"oracle_detail": "tests passed", "oracle_method": "code:exec"}, "origin": "real", "reference": "def count_samepair(list1,list2,list3):\n    result = sum(m == n == o for m, n, o in zip(list1,list2,list3))\n    return result", "reference_provenance": "MBPP reference solution", "rubric_id": "", "rubric_version": "", "schema_version": "1.0.0", "source": "MBPP", "source_license": "CC-BY-4.0", "task_class": "code", "task_input": "Write a function to count number items that are identical in the same position of three given lists."}
